  (prompt/new/30.md, STEP 9 correction — ROOT PURITY RULE, "Tam sıfırla",
  user confirmed) The STEP 9 (29.md) version above put concrete-instance
  Storage directories directly under `.sdd/decisions/` (root) — the exact
  mistake STEP 8 (25.md) already made and STEP 8 final (27.md) already
  corrected for TASKS. Applying that same correction here: the four
  Storage subdirectories were deleted (preserved in git history); DECISIONS'
  `role:` above was rewritten to describe it as ENGINE-only, with concrete
  decision instances routed through `../project/<domain>/decisions/
  <state>/*.sdd` instead; two new rules were added to `decisions.sdd`,
  `[D13]`/`[D14]`, mirroring `tasks.sdd`'s `[T19]`/`[T20]` (see
  ../decisions/decisions.sdd -> Note for the full reasoning). This is now
  the general ROOT PURITY RULE for `.sdd`: root holds only system-level
  (engine) definitions; project-specific knowledge, including any concrete
  instance storage, belongs under `project/<domain>/`, never directly
  under `.sdd` root. DECISIONS' entries in Relationships/Allowed/Forbidden
  did NOT change — only `role:` and the underlying directory layout moved.

  (prompt/new/31.md, STEP 9 enrichment — additive, Full Reset NOT required)
  DECISIONS' `path:` and its entries in Relationships/Allowed/Forbidden
  again did NOT change — only the `role:` field's rule range moved from
